---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const pageTitle = "Privacy Policy & Guarantee — 100% Client-Side Text Protection";
const pageDescription = "WordCountr Privacy Policy. Learn why WordCountr is 100% client-side: your text never leaves your device, is never logged, and is never used to train AI models.";
---

<Layout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  canonicalSlug="privacy"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-16">
    
    <div class="mono-eyebrow inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-[#0070f3]/25 bg-[#0070f3]/10 px-3 py-1 text-[#0070f3] mb-4">
      <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#0070f3]"></span>
      <span>Zero-Transmission Architecture</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed]">
      Privacy Policy & Guarantee
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-3 text-sm sm:text-base text-[#8f8f8f] leading-relaxed">
      At WordCountr, we believe writers should never have to surrender their privacy or trade unpublished manuscripts just to calculate word counts and readability.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1a1]">
      
      <div class="rounded-[10px] border border-[#0070f3]/30 bg-[#0070f3]/5 dark:bg-[#0070f3]/10 p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0070f3] mb-2 tracking-tight">The Architectural Rule: 100% Client-Side Execution</h2>
        <p class="text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed]">
          Every analytical feature in WordCountr — from real-time word counting and syllable estimation to DOCX parsing, PDF extraction, and keyword density calculations — runs <strong>exclusively inside your browser's local JavaScript environment</strong>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-[#0070f3]">
          Zero words, zero characters, and zero file contents are ever sent over the network to any server.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="vercel-card p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-1.5 tracking-tight">1. No AI Scraping on Your Writing</h3>
          <p>
            Many online writing tools secretly cache user submissions to fine-tune generative language models. We do not do this. Because your text is never transmitted to a server, it is mathematically impossible for us or any third party to scrape or train AI on your work.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-1.5 tracking-tight">2. Local Storage Auto-Save Only</h3>
          <p>
            To prevent accidental loss when you refresh or close a tab, WordCountr saves your working draft to your browser's native <code>localStorage</code> API. This data resides strictly on your physical machine and can be cleared instantly at any time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-1.5 tracking-tight">3. In-Browser DOCX and PDF Extraction</h3>
          <p>
            When you drag and drop a Microsoft Word or PDF document into WordCountr, the document is read into browser RAM using local JavaScript libraries (Mammoth.js and PDF.js). The file is parsed without triggering an HTTP upload request.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-1.5 tracking-tight">4. Zero Invasive Analytics</h3>
          <p>
            We do not track keystrokes, personal identities, IP addresses, or writing behavior. WordCountr operates as a pure software utility.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
